## Engines

Bundled with the installer:

| Component | License | Project |
|---|---|---|
| rhwp | MIT | https://github.com/edwardkim/rhwp |
| 7-Zip (console: `7z.exe`, `7z.dll`) | GNU LGPL-2.1-or-later; parts of `7z.dll`: LGPL with the unRAR license restriction, BSD-3-Clause, BSD-2-Clause | https://www.7-zip.org |
| Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable (Windows: next to `Filee.exe` and `rhwp.exe`, conda-forge `vc14_runtime`) | Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable license | https://github.com/conda-forge/vc-feedstock |

The Linux packages contain an rhwp built by Filee's CI from the unmodified source of the same release (tag `v0.8.7`,
commit `1a76570e833917d15817415a53c09ad61ab3203f`, `cargo build --release --locked --bin rhwp` on Ubuntu 22.04), so it
runs on older Linux systems than rhwp's own Linux build. The Windows ARM64 build contains an rhwp built the same way
on Windows ARM64 (with the C runtime linked statically), as rhwp has no ARM64 release. Both are under the same MIT
license; its `LICENSE` is next to them (`engines/rhwp`). Windows x64 and macOS use rhwp's release builds.

Unhwp's NuGet package has no native library for Linux ARM64 and Windows ARM64. Those builds contain one built by
Filee's CI from the unmodified source the package was built from (commit `405b17e137b3ca06299dcbc8a156599ac7027e91`,
`cargo build --release --locked -p unhwp --lib --features ffi`), under Unhwp's MIT license.

7-Zip is Copyright (C) 1999-2026 Igor Pavlov; its `License.txt` is installed next to it (`engines/7zip`). The RAR
decompression code in `7z.dll` is under the unRAR license restriction: it may be used to unpack RAR archives, but not
to develop a RAR (WinRAR) compatible archiver or to re-create the RAR compression algorithm. Filee only reads RAR
files. Source code: https://github.com/ip7z/7zip.

Downloaded from their official release pages when the user chooses to install them
(pinned in `src/Filee.Engines/Infrastructure/engines.json`):

| Component | License | Project |
|---|---|---|
| LibreOffice | MPL-2.0 | https://www.libreoffice.org |
| H2Orestart (HWP/HWPX import for LibreOffice) | GPL-3.0 | https://github.com/ebandal/H2Orestart |
| Eclipse Temurin JRE (for H2Orestart) | GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception | https://adoptium.net |
| Pandoc | GPL-2.0-or-later | https://github.com/jgm/pandoc |
| Ghostscript (conda-forge build) | AGPL-3.0 | https://www.ghostscript.com, https://github.com/conda-forge/ghostscript-feedstock |
| Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable (for Ghostscript, conda-forge `vc14_runtime`) | Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable license | https://github.com/conda-forge/vc-feedstock |
| FFmpeg 9.0.2 (gyan.dev "full_build-shared" Windows build; ffmpeg.exe, ffprobe.exe and their libraries, incl. x264, x265, libvpx, LAME, Opus, Vorbis, Theora, OpenCORE AMR) | GPL-3.0-or-later (the build is configured with `--enable-gpl --enable-version3`); FFmpeg itself LGPL-2.1-or-later | https://ffmpeg.org, build: https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/ (source: https://github.com/GyanD/codexffmpeg) |
| calibre (ebook-convert) | GPL-3.0 | https://calibre-ebook.com |
| Tesseract OCR 5.4 (UB Mannheim Windows build, with Leptonica and the MinGW libraries it ships; their notices are in its `doc` folder) | Apache-2.0 (Tesseract); Leptonica BSD-2-Clause; others as listed in the build | https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract, build: https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract |
| Tesseract language data (tessdata_fast 4.1.0), downloaded per language when used | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast |
| whisper.cpp (whisper-cli.exe Windows build) | MIT | https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp |
| ggml Whisper base model (`ggml-base.bin`) | MIT | https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp |

These programs run as separate processes. Their source code is available from the linked projects.

## Windows 11 Explorer menu (FileeExplorerMenu.dll)

The DLL is Filee's own C code, compiled with the Zig toolchain (a build tool, not shipped) against the mingw-w64
Windows headers, without a C runtime. Pieces of these projects that can end up in the binary:

| Component | License | Project |
|---|---|---|
| Zig compiler_rt (compiler support routines) | MIT | https://github.com/ziglang/zig |
| mingw-w64 Windows headers and import library definitions | Public domain / ZPL-2.1 | https://www.mingw-w64.org |

## Installer

`Filee-<version>-win-Setup.exe` is Filee's own installer (`src/Filee.Setup`, MIT like the app). It contains the
.NET runtime, Avalonia, SkiaSharp, HarfBuzzSharp, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm and SharpCompress (LZMA) listed in this file,
the x86 branch filter of the LZMA SDK (public domain, Igor Pavlov, https://www.7-zip.org/sdk.html), and the published
app as its payload. Filee 1.x's installer was built with Inno Setup, which is no longer used.

## Fonts and icons

| Component | License | Project |
|---|---|---|
| Noto Sans, Noto Sans Arabic, Noto Sans JP, Noto Sans KR, Noto Sans SC, Noto Sans Devanagari, Noto Sans Thai | SIL Open Font License 1.1 | https://github.com/notofonts |
| Test fonts in `tests/Filee.Engines.Tests/Fonts` (subsets of Noto Sans and Noto Sans KR; not shipped) | SIL Open Font License 1.1 | see `OFL.txt` in that folder |
| Material Design Icons (Pictogrammers) | Apache-2.0 | https://pictogrammers.com |
| Simple Icons 16.35.0 (GitHub Sponsors, Patreon, Ko-fi and PayPal logos in the Sponsor window) | CC0-1.0 | https://simpleicons.org |

The GitHub Sponsors, Patreon, Ko-fi and PayPal names and logos are trademarks of their owners and are used only to link
to each service.

## Documentation theme examples

The optional JSON recipes in `docs/themes/` adapt palette data from Catppuccin, Nord, Dracula and VS Code's classic
Monokai theme. Their source links, colour adjustments and copyright/license notices are in
[docs/themes/NOTICE.md](docs/themes/NOTICE.md). These are documentation examples, not runtime dependencies.
HONEYCOMB_LICENSE
printf 'APPL????' > "$HC_BUNDLE/Contents/PkgInfo"
/usr/bin/codesign --force --deep --sign - "$HC_BUNDLE"
/usr/bin/codesign --verify --deep --strict "$HC_BUNDLE"

if ! hc_setup_extended; then
    echo "Extended format setup failed. Core conversions and native editors are ready."
    echo "To retry extended formats, run: /bin/bash \"$0\" --extended-only"
fi

HC_NEEDS_SUDO=0
hc_privileged() {
    if [ "$HC_NEEDS_SUDO" -eq 1 ]; then /usr/bin/sudo "$@"; else "$@"; fi
}
if [ ! -w /Applications ] || { [ -e "$HC_APP" ] && [ ! -w "$HC_APP" ]; }; then
    echo "Administrator access is needed to replace /Applications/Honeycomb.app."
    /usr/bin/sudo -v
    HC_NEEDS_SUDO=1
fi
# Replace only our bundle, and keep a rollback copy until the installed signature verifies.
if [ -e "$HC_APP" ]; then
    if [ ! -f "$HC_APP/Contents/Info.plist" ] || [ "$(/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy -c 'Print :CFBundleIdentifier' "$HC_APP/Contents/Info.plist" 2>/dev/null || true)" != "app.honeycomb.personal" ]; then
        echo "A different app already occupies $HC_APP. Rename or move it before installing."
        false
    fi
fi
HC_NEW_PATH="/Applications/.Honeycomb-install-$$.app"
hc_privileged /bin/mkdir "$HC_NEW_PATH"
HC_DEST_STAGE="$HC_NEW_PATH"
hc_privileged /usr/bin/ditto "$HC_BUNDLE" "$HC_DEST_STAGE"
/usr/bin/codesign --verify --deep --strict "$HC_DEST_STAGE"
HC_PREVIOUS_CDHASH=""
if [ -d "$HC_APP" ]; then HC_PREVIOUS_CDHASH=$(hc_bundle_cdhash "$HC_APP" || true); fi
hc_stop_honeycomb
if [ -e "$HC_APP" ]; then
    HC_BACKUP_PATH="/Applications/.Honeycomb-backup-$$.app"
    if [ -e "$HC_BACKUP_PATH" ]; then echo "A rollback path already exists: $HC_BACKUP_PATH"; false; fi
    hc_privileged /bin/mv "$HC_APP" "$HC_BACKUP_PATH"
    HC_BACKUP="$HC_BACKUP_PATH"
fi
hc_privileged /bin/mv "$HC_DEST_STAGE" "$HC_APP"
HC_DEST_STAGE=""
hc_privileged /usr/bin/codesign --force --deep --sign - /Applications/Honeycomb.app
/usr/bin/codesign --verify --deep --strict /Applications/Honeycomb.app
HC_COMPLETE=1
/bin/mv -f "$HC_STAGE/main.swift" "$HC_BASE/main.swift"
if [ -n "$HC_BACKUP" ]; then hc_privileged /bin/rm -rf "$HC_BACKUP"; HC_BACKUP=""; fi

HC_AGENT_DIR="$HOME/Library/LaunchAgents"
HC_AGENT="$HC_AGENT_DIR/app.honeycomb.personal.plist"
/bin/mkdir -p "$HC_AGENT_DIR"
/usr/bin/launchctl bootout "gui/$(/usr/bin/id -u)/app.honeycomb.personal" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
HC_LOGIN=$(/usr/bin/plutil -extract startAtLogin raw -o - "$HC_BASE/config.json" 2>/dev/null || echo true)
if [ "$HC_LOGIN" = "true" ] || [ "$HC_LOGIN" = "1" ]; then
cat > "$HC_AGENT" <<'HONEYCOMB_AGENT'
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
<key>Label</key><string>app.honeycomb.personal</string>
<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/usr/bin/open</string><string>-g</string><string>/Applications/Honeycomb.app</string><string>--args</string><string>--background</string></array>
<key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
<key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key><string>Aqua</string>
</dict></plist>
HONEYCOMB_AGENT
/bin/chmod 644 "$HC_AGENT"
echo "Start at login enabled. Honeycomb will open silently at your next login."
else
    /bin/rm -f "$HC_AGENT"
fi
if [ -x /System/Library/Frameworks/CoreServices.framework/Frameworks/LaunchServices.framework/Support/lsregister ]; then
    /System/Library/Frameworks/CoreServices.framework/Frameworks/LaunchServices.framework/Support/lsregister -f "$HC_APP" || true
fi
HC_NEW_CDHASH=$(hc_bundle_cdhash "$HC_APP" || true)
if [ -n "$HC_PREVIOUS_CDHASH" ] && [ -n "$HC_NEW_CDHASH" ] && [ "$HC_PREVIOUS_CDHASH" != "$HC_NEW_CDHASH" ]; then
    hc_reset_permission Accessibility Accessibility || true
    hc_reset_permission ListenEvent "Input Monitoring" || true
fi
hc_launch_for_permissions Privacy_Accessibility --request-accessibility --request-input-monitoring
echo
echo "Honeycomb is installed and running in the background."
echo "Open its settings from the hexagon menu bar icon. Close or minimize keeps it running."
echo "Settings: $HC_BASE/config.json — changes reload automatically."
echo "Logs: $HC_BASE/log.txt"
echo "Select a desktop file. With the default shortcut, hold Option + Space, move the pointer, then release over a format."
echo "Change the shortcut from the hexagon menu bar icon > Open Honeycomb > Shortcut."
echo "Release over More for another ring of hexes. Click a tool, More, or Back. Escape cancels."
echo "Allow notifications when asked, for completion messages and Show in Finder."
echo "If either permission still shows an old entry, run this installer with --repair-accessibility or --repair-input-monitoring."
echo
echo "Grant these permissions to /Applications/Honeycomb.app:"
echo "  Accessibility: System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility > Honeycomb ON"
echo "  Input Monitoring: System Settings > Privacy & Security > Input Monitoring > Honeycomb ON"
echo "  Automation > Finder: System Settings > Privacy & Security > Automation > Honeycomb > Finder ON"
